{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"e2332e494ebd91e8e08972d3296eaef822a65d0ed915b91fbe0d075cd77763ca","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP server tool output serialization","key_entities":["src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","src/rebar/mcp_server.py","src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py","time.time_ns()","created_at","updated_at","timestamp","signed_at","comments[].timestamp","attestations.*.signed_at","signature.signed_at","TicketStateOut","list_tickets","ready_tickets","show_ticket","plan_review_status","sign_result","verify_signature_result","Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER","2**53-1"],"problem_keywords":["json serialization","bigint","nanosecond timestamps","javascript interoperability","ieee-754 precision","mcp tool output","rfc 8259 compliance"],"propositions":["MCP server emits nanosecond-precision timestamps (19-digit integers from time.time_ns()) as bare JSON numbers, which exceed RFC 8259 §6 interoperable range [-(2**53)+1, (2**53)-1] and truncate silently when parsed by IEEE-754 binary64 clients","JavaScript MCP clients with lossless JSON parsing materialize out-of-safe-range numbers as BigInt, causing JSON.stringify to throw TypeError when re-serializing tool results","Ticket state models in _mcp_models.py with extra='allow' pass undeclared timestamp fields as Python int, and nested raw-dict fields (comments, attestations, signatures) carry unvalidated ns timestamps directly to the wire","list_tickets, ready_tickets, and other tools returning ticket records fail with BigInt serialization error while tools emitting no timestamp fields succeed, splitting the tool population by presence of ns timestamps","The fix must emit out-of-range integers as exact decimal strings at the MCP tool-return boundary only, preserving Python int throughout the store and internal code, and must widen typed schema declarations to accept int|str for backward compatibility with clients using plain JSON.parse"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787908185850266001,"uuid":"507651a0-6a71-486a-96d0-4bab48f861fe"}